        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hi! Thank you for the quick answer.\r\nI was thinking if it would be possible to access the winbar remaining after having removed the buffers. In that sense, I was thinking about an option of creating a dummy file when no more buffers are left on my window layout.\r\n\r\nWhat I was trying to achieve is to customize the window bar after all buffers are removed. I would need a way of explicitly get an event on winenter/bufenter when all the buffers are removed, a way of setting a pattern on that event for that concrete window\r\n\r\nThank you! ",
